From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Fri, 05 Jun 2026 12:00:00 -0700
Subject: net: airoha: ppe: guard NULL FOE entry in multicast handler

airoha_ppe_foe_get_entry_locked() returns NULL when the PPE SRAM read times
out. arht_ppe_multicast_handler() passed that pointer straight to
arht_multicast_hwnat_data_handler_hook(), which dereferences it via
ppe_is_multicast_entry(), so a timed-out lookup faults. Bail out when the
entry could not be read.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/arht_ppe.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/arht_ppe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/arht_ppe.c
@@ -554,6 +554,11 @@ int arht_ppe_multicast_handler(struct ai
 		hwe = airoha_ppe_foe_get_entry_locked(ppe, foe_index);
 		spin_unlock_bh(&ppe_lock);
 
+		/* SRAM read can time out and return NULL; the hook dereferences
+		 * hwe (ppe_is_multicast_entry) without checking.
+		 */
+		if (!hwe)
+			return 0;
 		arht_multicast_hwnat_data_handler_hook(hwe, skb);
 	}
 	return 0;
